      "README.md": "# OGENIC WAVE Runner-1 — Certificate & Runtime Evidence\n\nGenerated: 2026-10-18 (Asia/Bangkok)\n\nThis package is the owner-retained evidence set for OGE-128. It contains no raw token, password, private key, cookie, OAuth file, or Codex authentication file.\n\n## Current truth\n\n- GitHub primary `Ogenicchocolate21debug`: **PASS / admin**.\n- GitHub secondary `Wave-Runner-2`: **PASS / write**.\n- Existing Actions service: **PASS / `wave-runner-01` / one service**.\n- Codex `GPT_GS_CODEX`: **PASS / signed in under runner user `wave`**.\n- Codex `GPT_TS_CODEX`: **BLOCKED AT ROOT SSH AUTHORIZATION**. `SSH_PRIVATE_KEY` was decrypted with the owner-designated `SSH_KEY` passphrase fallback and loaded into `ssh-agent`, but `root@127.0.0.1` rejected the corresponding public key.\n- WAVE Command source path: **SOURCE VERIFIED**. `/api/wave/command` performs owner confirmation, dispatches `wave-command-consumer.yml` to Runner-1, runs `codex exec`, and posts a result receipt.\n- WAVE Command live E2E: **NOT YET PROVEN**. The live `/command` page requires Owner sign-in and no completed Command Consumer receipt has been captured in this package.\n\n## Certificate policy\n\nThe owner authorization record is permanent until explicitly revoked. A cryptographic leaf certificate is not made non-expiring: it must be short-lived and automatically renewed. This prevents a stolen private key from becoming permanent access.\n\n- Authorization record: `PERMANENT_UNTIL_REVOKED`\n- X.509 leaf maximum: 397 days\n- Automatic renewal window: 30 days before expiry\n- Revocation: immediate through Infisical Certificate Manager / Yellow Stone authority\n\n## Exact evidence\n\n- Certificate Manager access: GitHub Actions run `39030482640`, job `117403600915`.\n- Runner/Codex GS proof: run `39115866114`, job `117641403648`.\n- Encrypted private-key detection: run `39117947367`, job `117647457443`, artifact `12133197026`, digest `sha256:ee5e3d468d4c6108f0131fd8547f6f86ead2c803e9723ec785e98909fe3d086e`.\n- SSH encrypted-key support commit: `11ebb06ec1a999f884d75ba9c8e8d0e93bf4724b`.\n- Key/passphrase pairing and root authorization result: run `39118118283`, job `117647963926`, commit `9ccc591dd2cea7d3a54abe1bc2894f8880b33671`, artifact `12133310952`, digest `sha256:a72dcf170bb9c310f35335a0973582f5719c9bbff4622a4880f64f8a8e3950a4`. Key loaded successfully; root rejected public-key authentication.\n- Manual re-run attempt #2 of run `39118118283`, job `117648861899`, artifact `12133665511`, digest `sha256:1f4f27f0935dc059f1d744d16c50208b55fffd8560b2b212f0a01abaec77cddb`. The key again decrypted and loaded successfully; root again rejected public-key authentication.\n- Draft PR: `https://github.com/Ogenicchocolate21debug/Build-Platform/pull/41`.\n\n## Next runtime closure\n\n1. Authorize the matching public key for root on Runner-1, or explicitly allow this key through the host SSH policy. Do not paste the private key or passphrase in chat.\n2. Re-run `WAVE Owner — Runner-1 Terminal & Dual Codex Identity Proof` on the task branch. The workflow already supports the owner-designated `SSH_KEY` passphrase fallback.\n3. Accept GPT-TS only if the root proof reports `GPT_TS_CODEX` signed in without exposing authentication material.\n4. Sign in to WAVE Owner Access and execute one bounded read-only Command. Accept the workflow only after the UI shows a real task/run ID and the backend records `COMMAND_RESULT_DONE`.\n",
